  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Increasing the Capacity of Russian nature Reserves and parks to conserve Imperiled Habitats and Species</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project provides funding for scientific field work within the Wrangel Island Federal Biosphere Reserve in Russia specifically pertaining to the population of snow geese shared with the United States. Additionally, the proposal will fund a small grants competition for Russian nature reserves and parks. USFWS and the recipient will work collaboratively on advertising the grants competition to Russias nature reserves and parks, receiving and translating proposals. The recipient will organize one proposal review panel in Russia, and USFWS will organize one review panel in the United States. Funding decisions will be made jointly between USFWS and ANO Ekosentr Zapovedniki, and USFWS will have final approval for all final funding decisions. USFWS and ANO Ekosentr Zapovedniki will communicate with the sub-grantees and collaboratively monitor technical and administrative performance. Sub-grants funded by this award will improve the protected areas law enforcement, visitor center services, reserve management, and biodiversity conservation through training courses, the purchase of patrolling equipment, and the increased presence of law enforcement officers. Species to benefit include the critically endangered saiga antelope, Amur tiger, polar bear, walrus, Far Eastern leopard, snow goose, and Asiatic black bear.</narrative>
  </description>
